{"v":1,"book":"gita","n":13,"title":"Creation and the creator","narrator":{"name":"Brian","voice":"en-US-BrianMultilingualNeural"},"duration":316.056,"scenes":[{"layout":"title","headline":"Creation and the Creator","visual":["The field, and the one who knows it"],"L":[],"say":"Chapter Thirteen. Creation and the Creator. Krishna now separates two things we usually mix up: the body, and the one who knows it.","start":0.0,"at":0.576,"end":10.536,"words":[[0.05,0.388,"Chapter"],[0.45,0.675,"Thirteen"],[1.512,0.675,"Creation"],[2.2,0.175,"and"],[2.388,0.087,"the"],[2.487,0.662,"Creator"],[3.55,0.4,"Krishna"],[3.962,0.237,"now"],[4.213,0.55,"separates"],[4.775,0.188,"two"],[4.975,0.3,"things"],[5.287,0.113,"we"],[5.412,0.4,"usually"],[5.825,0.287,"mix"],[6.125,0.338,"up"],[6.838,0.163,"the"],[7.013,0.475,"body"],[7.513,0.175,"and"],[7.7,0.087,"the"],[7.8,0.188,"one"],[8.0,0.138,"who"],[8.15,0.3,"knows"],[8.463,0.25,"it"]]},{"layout":"verse","headline":"","visual":[],"L":["L1"],"ref":"13.01","verse":"The Supreme Lord said: O Arjuna, this physical body, a miniature universe, may be called the creation. One who knows the creation is called the creator by the seers of truth.","key":false,"vs":[24,55],"say":"In many translations this is called the field and the knower of the field. Our book uses the words creation and creator. Verse one. The Supreme Lord said: O Arjuna, this physical body, a miniature universe, may be called the creation. One who knows the creation is called the creator by the seers of truth.","start":10.536,"at":11.112,"end":33.888,"words":[[0.1,0.138,"In"],[0.25,0.237,"many"],[0.5,0.838,"translations"],[1.35,0.2,"this"],[1.562,0.113,"is"],[1.688,0.287,"called"],[1.988,0.075,"the"],[2.075,0.575,"field"],[2.675,0.15,"and"],[2.837,0.087,"the"],[2.938,0.45,"knower"],[3.4,0.113,"of"],[3.525,0.087,"the"],[3.625,0.525,"field"],[4.525,0.15,"Our"],[4.688,0.287,"book"],[4.987,0.45,"uses"],[5.45,0.113,"the"],[5.575,0.338,"words"],[5.925,0.625,"creation"],[6.562,0.163,"and"],[6.737,0.625,"creator"],[7.75,0.275,"Verse"],[8.037,0.35,"one"],[8.775,0.062,"The"],[8.85,0.487,"Supreme"],[9.35,0.3,"Lord"],[9.662,0.412,"said"],[10.662,0.225,"O"],[10.9,0.688,"Arjuna"],[12.037,0.225,"this"],[12.275,0.438,"physical"],[12.725,0.487,"body"],[13.55,0.1,"a"],[13.662,0.45,"miniature"],[14.125,0.637,"universe"],[15.125,0.188,"may"],[15.325,0.113,"be"],[15.45,0.312,"called"],[15.775,0.062,"the"],[15.85,0.65,"creation"],[16.913,0.287,"One"],[17.212,0.188,"who"],[17.413,0.362,"knows"],[17.788,0.1,"the"],[17.9,0.55,"creation"],[18.462,0.15,"is"],[18.625,0.325,"called"],[18.962,0.075,"the"],[19.05,0.537,"creator"],[19.6,0.163,"by"],[19.775,0.087,"the"],[19.875,0.438,"seers"],[20.325,0.087,"of"],[20.425,0.537,"truth"]]},{"layout":"verse","headline":"","visual":[],"L":["L1"],"ref":"13.02","verse":"O Arjuna, know Me to be the creator of all the creation. The true understanding of both the creator and the creation is considered by Me to be the spiritual or metaphysical knowledge.","key":true,"vs":[9,42],"say":"And Krishna says where real knowledge lies. Verse two. O Arjuna, know Me to be the creator of all the creation. The true understanding of both the creator and the creation is considered by Me to be the spiritual or metaphysical knowledge.","start":33.888,"at":34.464,"end":51.12,"words":[[0.05,0.125,"And"],[0.188,0.4,"Krishna"],[0.6,0.375,"says"],[0.988,0.275,"where"],[1.275,0.25,"real"],[1.538,0.438,"knowledge"],[1.988,0.438,"lies"],[2.825,0.263,"Verse"],[3.1,0.325,"two"],[3.825,0.113,"O"],[3.95,0.675,"Arjuna"],[5.088,0.225,"know"],[5.325,0.138,"Me"],[5.475,0.138,"to"],[5.625,0.188,"be"],[5.825,0.1,"the"],[5.938,0.6,"creator"],[6.55,0.125,"of"],[6.688,0.212,"all"],[6.912,0.087,"the"],[7.013,0.65,"creation"],[8.075,0.075,"The"],[8.162,0.35,"true"],[8.525,0.688,"understanding"],[9.225,0.163,"of"],[9.4,0.312,"both"],[9.725,0.087,"the"],[9.825,0.625,"creator"],[10.463,0.113,"and"],[10.588,0.075,"the"],[10.675,0.5,"creation"],[11.188,0.15,"is"],[11.35,0.5,"considered"],[11.863,0.163,"by"],[12.037,0.3,"Me"],[12.35,0.138,"to"],[12.5,0.188,"be"],[12.7,0.087,"the"],[12.8,0.713,"spiritual"],[13.525,0.163,"or"],[13.7,0.588,"metaphysical"],[14.3,0.55,"knowledge"]]},{"layout":"story","headline":"What the field is made of","visual":["Nature, intellect, ego, the five elements","The ten organs, the mind, the sense objects","Desire, hatred, pleasure, pain"],"L":["L1"],"say":"He lists what belongs to the creation, the field: primal nature, the cosmic intellect, the ego, the five elements, the ten organs, the mind, and the five objects of the senses. And then, surprisingly, he adds desire, hatred, pleasure and pain. Even our feelings are part of the field. The one who knows them is not.","start":51.12,"at":51.696,"end":73.176,"words":[[0.163,0.163,"He"],[0.338,0.35,"lists"],[0.7,0.163,"what"],[0.875,0.438,"belongs"],[1.325,0.1,"to"],[1.438,0.075,"the"],[1.525,0.55,"creation"],[2.1,0.1,"the"],[2.212,0.487,"field"],[3.038,0.362,"primal"],[3.413,0.425,"nature"],[3.862,0.087,"the"],[3.962,0.425,"cosmic"],[4.4,0.5,"intellect"],[4.925,0.062,"the"],[5.0,0.5,"ego"],[5.525,0.1,"the"],[5.638,0.287,"five"],[5.938,0.463,"elements"],[6.425,0.087,"the"],[6.525,0.225,"ten"],[6.763,0.463,"organs"],[7.25,0.087,"the"],[7.35,0.5,"mind"],[8.162,0.188,"and"],[8.363,0.087,"the"],[8.463,0.3,"five"],[8.775,0.412,"objects"],[9.2,0.075,"of"],[9.287,0.075,"the"],[9.375,0.562,"senses"],[10.3,0.138,"And"],[10.45,0.388,"then"],[11.125,0.875,"surprisingly"],[12.012,0.212,"he"],[12.238,0.263,"adds"],[12.512,0.65,"desire"],[13.375,0.637,"hatred"],[14.287,0.512,"pleasure"],[14.812,0.125,"and"],[14.95,0.463,"pain"],[15.812,0.263,"Even"],[16.087,0.15,"our"],[16.25,0.575,"feelings"],[16.837,0.175,"are"],[17.025,0.263,"part"],[17.3,0.087,"of"],[17.4,0.087,"the"],[17.5,0.525,"field"],[18.425,0.087,"The"],[18.525,0.25,"one"],[18.788,0.188,"who"],[18.988,0.35,"knows"],[19.35,0.237,"them"],[19.6,0.175,"is"],[19.788,0.463,"not"]]},{"layout":"verse","headline":"","visual":[],"L":["L2"],"ref":"13.07-08","verse":"Humility, modesty, nonviolence, forgiveness, honesty, service to guru, purity of thought, word, and deed, steadfastness, self-control; and aversion towards sense objects, absence of ego; constant reflection on pain and suffering inherent in birth, old age, disease, and death;","key":true,"vs":[21,59],"say":"Then Krishna gives a remarkable definition of knowledge. It is not a list of facts. It is a list of qualities. Humility, modesty, nonviolence, forgiveness, honesty, service to guru, purity of thought, word, and deed, steadfastness, self-control; and aversion towards sense objects, absence of ego; constant reflection on pain and suffering inherent in birth, old age, disease, and death;","start":73.176,"at":73.752,"end":105.672,"words":[[0.087,0.275,"Then"],[0.375,0.525,"Krishna"],[0.912,0.287,"gives"],[1.212,0.113,"a"],[1.337,0.65,"remarkable"],[2.0,0.637,"definition"],[2.65,0.15,"of"],[2.812,0.613,"knowledge"],[3.788,0.125,"It"],[3.925,0.125,"is"],[4.062,0.3,"not"],[4.388,0.1,"a"],[4.5,0.338,"list"],[4.85,0.1,"of"],[4.963,0.562,"facts"],[5.888,0.125,"It"],[6.025,0.138,"is"],[6.175,0.087,"a"],[6.275,0.338,"list"],[6.625,0.1,"of"],[6.737,0.725,"qualities"],[7.862,0.562,"Humility"],[8.975,0.588,"modesty"],[10.05,0.825,"nonviolence"],[11.275,0.613,"forgiveness"],[12.4,0.537,"honesty"],[13.488,0.388,"service"],[13.887,0.1,"to"],[14.0,0.45,"guru"],[14.988,0.35,"purity"],[15.35,0.087,"of"],[15.45,0.362,"thought"],[16.375,0.412,"word"],[17.175,0.15,"and"],[17.337,0.35,"deed"],[18.188,0.863,"steadfastness"],[19.425,0.762,"self-control"],[20.95,0.062,"and"],[21.025,0.412,"aversion"],[21.45,0.3,"towards"],[21.762,0.237,"sense"],[22.012,0.575,"objects"],[22.975,0.438,"absence"],[23.425,0.087,"of"],[23.525,0.362,"ego"],[24.688,0.412,"constant"],[25.113,0.475,"reflection"],[25.6,0.125,"on"],[25.738,0.4,"pain"],[26.15,0.1,"and"],[26.262,0.4,"suffering"],[26.675,0.412,"inherent"],[27.1,0.1,"in"],[27.212,0.375,"birth"],[28.113,0.2,"old"],[28.325,0.362,"age"],[28.988,0.537,"disease"],[29.538,0.163,"and"],[29.712,0.4,"death"]]},{"layout":"story","headline":"Hands and eyes everywhere","visual":["His hands, feet and eyes are everywhere","Inside and outside all beings","Very far away, and very near"],"L":["L3"],"say":"Krishna then describes the Supreme the only way it can be described: in paradox. His hands and feet, his eyes, heads and mouths are everywhere. He perceives without senses, sustains all without being attached. He is inside and outside all beings, moving and unmoving. He is too subtle to grasp, and so he is very far away, and very near.","start":105.672,"at":106.248,"end":129.624,"words":[[0.087,0.463,"Krishna"],[0.562,0.287,"then"],[0.863,0.625,"describes"],[1.5,0.087,"the"],[1.6,0.613,"Supreme"],[2.225,0.062,"the"],[2.3,0.325,"only"],[2.638,0.263,"way"],[2.913,0.113,"it"],[3.038,0.15,"can"],[3.2,0.113,"be"],[3.325,0.662,"described"],[4.013,0.163,"in"],[4.188,0.7,"paradox"],[5.3,0.15,"His"],[5.463,0.4,"hands"],[5.875,0.1,"and"],[5.987,0.362,"feet"],[6.362,0.263,"his"],[6.638,0.425,"eyes"],[7.075,0.4,"heads"],[7.487,0.113,"and"],[7.612,0.4,"mouths"],[8.025,0.163,"are"],[8.2,0.6,"everywhere"],[9.2,0.1,"He"],[9.312,0.575,"perceives"],[9.9,0.362,"without"],[10.275,0.65,"senses"],[11.338,0.637,"sustains"],[11.988,0.325,"all"],[12.325,0.35,"without"],[12.688,0.2,"being"],[12.9,0.613,"attached"],[13.912,0.175,"He"],[14.1,0.138,"is"],[14.25,0.6,"inside"],[14.863,0.125,"and"],[15.0,0.463,"outside"],[15.475,0.225,"all"],[15.713,0.45,"beings"],[16.188,0.525,"moving"],[16.725,0.125,"and"],[16.863,0.637,"unmoving"],[17.95,0.175,"He"],[18.137,0.15,"is"],[18.3,0.188,"too"],[18.5,0.35,"subtle"],[18.863,0.1,"to"],[18.975,0.575,"grasp"],[19.575,0.138,"and"],[19.725,0.2,"so"],[19.938,0.163,"he"],[20.113,0.113,"is"],[20.238,0.263,"very"],[20.512,0.263,"far"],[20.788,0.438,"away"],[21.25,0.163,"and"],[21.425,0.275,"very"],[21.712,0.438,"near"]]},{"layout":"verse","headline":"","visual":[],"L":["L4"],"ref":"13.21","verse":"Purusha enjoys three modes of material Nature (Prakriti) by associating with Prakriti. Attachment to the Gunas due to ignorance caused by previous Karma is the cause of birth of living entity (jiva) in good and evil wombs.","key":true,"vs":[10,47],"say":"Why, then, are we born again and again? Verse twenty-one. Purusha enjoys three modes of material Nature (Prakriti) by associating with Prakriti. Attachment to the Gunas due to ignorance caused by previous Karma is the cause of birth of living entity (jiva) in good and evil wombs.","start":129.624,"at":130.2,"end":150.528,"words":[[0.075,0.263,"Why"],[0.35,0.362,"then"],[0.738,0.138,"are"],[0.887,0.163,"we"],[1.062,0.287,"born"],[1.363,0.4,"again"],[1.775,0.1,"and"],[1.887,0.45,"again"],[2.725,0.388,"Verse"],[3.125,0.738,"twenty-one"],[4.25,0.5,"Purusha"],[4.763,0.537,"enjoys"],[5.312,0.312,"three"],[5.638,0.412,"modes"],[6.062,0.125,"of"],[6.2,0.487,"material"],[6.7,0.512,"Nature"],[7.438,0.613,"Prakriti"],[8.65,0.175,"by"],[8.838,0.675,"associating"],[9.525,0.163,"with"],[9.7,0.588,"Prakriti"],[10.688,0.588,"Attachment"],[11.287,0.1,"to"],[11.4,0.087,"the"],[11.5,0.375,"Gunas"],[11.887,0.188,"due"],[12.088,0.138,"to"],[12.238,0.475,"ignorance"],[12.725,0.362,"caused"],[13.1,0.125,"by"],[13.238,0.438,"previous"],[13.688,0.463,"Karma"],[14.175,0.163,"is"],[14.35,0.1,"the"],[14.463,0.362,"cause"],[14.838,0.125,"of"],[14.975,0.312,"birth"],[15.3,0.125,"of"],[15.438,0.3,"living"],[15.75,0.512,"entity"],[16.288,0.525,"jiva"],[17.025,0.225,"in"],[17.262,0.325,"good"],[17.6,0.113,"and"],[17.725,0.312,"evil"],[18.05,0.463,"wombs"]]},{"layout":"verse","headline":"","visual":[],"L":["L5"],"ref":"13.27","verse":"The one who sees the same eternal Supreme Lord dwelling as Spirit equally within all mortal beings, truly sees.","key":true,"vs":[9,28],"say":"And what does true sight look like? Verse twenty-seven. The one who sees the same eternal Supreme Lord dwelling as Spirit equally within all mortal beings, truly sees.","start":150.528,"at":151.104,"end":163.488,"words":[[0.05,0.175,"And"],[0.237,0.15,"what"],[0.4,0.138,"does"],[0.55,0.225,"true"],[0.787,0.375,"sight"],[1.175,0.237,"look"],[1.425,0.4,"like"],[2.212,0.388,"Verse"],[2.612,0.85,"twenty-seven"],[3.862,0.1,"The"],[3.975,0.237,"one"],[4.225,0.138,"who"],[4.375,0.412,"sees"],[4.8,0.087,"the"],[4.9,0.338,"same"],[5.25,0.375,"eternal"],[5.638,0.55,"Supreme"],[6.2,0.275,"Lord"],[6.487,0.463,"dwelling"],[6.963,0.125,"as"],[7.1,0.45,"Spirit"],[7.575,0.438,"equally"],[8.025,0.3,"within"],[8.338,0.225,"all"],[8.575,0.325,"mortal"],[8.912,0.512,"beings"],[9.675,0.362,"truly"],[10.05,0.512,"sees"]]},{"layout":"story","headline":"Space is never stained","visual":["As space is not tainted by what fills it","So the Spirit is not tainted by the body","As one sun lights the whole world"],"L":[],"say":"Krishna ends with two images. Just as all-pervading space is never stained by what moves within it, the Spirit dwelling in every body is never stained. And just as one sun lights up the whole world, the one Spirit lights up the whole of creation.","start":163.488,"at":164.064,"end":180.72,"words":[[0.062,0.438,"Krishna"],[0.512,0.362,"ends"],[0.887,0.188,"with"],[1.087,0.212,"two"],[1.312,0.575,"images"],[2.288,0.312,"Just"],[2.612,0.113,"as"],[2.737,0.6,"all-pervading"],[3.35,0.438,"space"],[3.8,0.125,"is"],[3.938,0.275,"never"],[4.225,0.487,"stained"],[4.725,0.175,"by"],[4.912,0.188,"what"],[5.112,0.362,"moves"],[5.487,0.3,"within"],[5.8,0.25,"it"],[6.6,0.113,"the"],[6.725,0.45,"Spirit"],[7.188,0.45,"dwelling"],[7.65,0.15,"in"],[7.812,0.275,"every"],[8.1,0.388,"body"],[8.5,0.138,"is"],[8.65,0.263,"never"],[8.925,0.525,"stained"],[9.85,0.113,"And"],[9.975,0.263,"just"],[10.25,0.113,"as"],[10.375,0.237,"one"],[10.625,0.35,"sun"],[10.988,0.338,"lights"],[11.338,0.163,"up"],[11.512,0.075,"the"],[11.6,0.275,"whole"],[11.887,0.5,"world"],[12.912,0.15,"the"],[13.075,0.225,"one"],[13.312,0.425,"Spirit"],[13.75,0.35,"lights"],[14.125,0.175,"up"],[14.312,0.075,"the"],[14.4,0.287,"whole"],[14.7,0.1,"of"],[14.812,0.613,"creation"]]},{"layout":"lesson","headline":"The Body Is the Field; the Soul Is the Knower of the Field","visual":["The body, mind, ego and senses: the field","The eternal Spirit: the knower","Wisdom begins by telling them apart"],"L":["L1"],"say":"Lesson one. The body is the field; the soul is the knower of the field. The body, with its mind, ego, senses and everything they meet, is the field. The eternal Spirit that perceives it is the knower. Wisdom begins by telling the two apart.","start":180.72,"at":181.296,"end":199.176,"words":[[0.062,0.35,"Lesson"],[0.425,0.375,"one"],[1.2,0.087,"The"],[1.3,0.412,"body"],[1.725,0.163,"is"],[1.9,0.1,"the"],[2.013,0.575,"field"],[3.0,0.113,"the"],[3.125,0.45,"soul"],[3.587,0.175,"is"],[3.775,0.1,"the"],[3.888,0.463,"knower"],[4.362,0.1,"of"],[4.475,0.087,"the"],[4.575,0.512,"field"],[5.475,0.087,"The"],[5.575,0.45,"body"],[6.05,0.175,"with"],[6.237,0.15,"its"],[6.4,0.525,"mind"],[7.088,0.475,"ego"],[7.575,0.6,"senses"],[8.188,0.15,"and"],[8.35,0.438,"everything"],[8.8,0.125,"they"],[8.938,0.362,"meet"],[9.75,0.188,"is"],[9.95,0.1,"the"],[10.062,0.525,"field"],[10.963,0.062,"The"],[11.037,0.425,"eternal"],[11.475,0.55,"Spirit"],[12.037,0.188,"that"],[12.238,0.537,"perceives"],[12.787,0.188,"it"],[12.988,0.2,"is"],[13.2,0.087,"the"],[13.3,0.525,"knower"],[14.225,0.425,"Wisdom"],[14.662,0.487,"begins"],[15.162,0.175,"by"],[15.35,0.425,"telling"],[15.787,0.087,"the"],[15.887,0.212,"two"],[16.113,0.537,"apart"]]},{"layout":"lesson","headline":"True Knowledge Is Characterized by Humility and Spiritual Virtues","visual":["Humility, nonviolence, forgiveness, honesty","Purity, steadiness, self-control","Knowledge is a way of being"],"L":["L2"],"say":"Lesson two. True knowledge is marked by humility and spiritual virtues. Real knowledge is not information. It is a way of being: humble, honest, nonviolent, forgiving, pure, steady and self-controlled, devoted, and calm in good times and bad.","start":199.176,"at":199.752,"end":220.08,"words":[[0.062,0.338,"Lesson"],[0.412,0.375,"two"],[1.188,0.212,"True"],[1.413,0.5,"knowledge"],[1.938,0.163,"is"],[2.112,0.425,"marked"],[2.55,0.163,"by"],[2.725,0.713,"humility"],[3.45,0.15,"and"],[3.612,0.575,"spiritual"],[4.2,0.625,"virtues"],[5.225,0.237,"Real"],[5.475,0.55,"knowledge"],[6.05,0.175,"is"],[6.237,0.312,"not"],[6.562,0.825,"information"],[7.787,0.075,"It"],[7.875,0.087,"is"],[7.975,0.062,"a"],[8.05,0.212,"way"],[8.275,0.1,"of"],[8.387,0.3,"being"],[9.4,0.375,"humble"],[10.363,0.45,"honest"],[11.188,0.738,"nonviolent"],[12.425,0.512,"forgiving"],[13.45,0.412,"pure"],[14.438,0.45,"steady"],[14.9,0.1,"and"],[15.012,0.8,"self-controlled"],[16.275,0.525,"devoted"],[17.238,0.125,"and"],[17.375,0.375,"calm"],[17.762,0.1,"in"],[17.875,0.212,"good"],[18.1,0.45,"times"],[18.562,0.113,"and"],[18.688,0.412,"bad"]]},{"layout":"lesson","headline":"God Is Omnipresent Yet Beyond All Description","visual":["No fixed form, yet perceiving through all","Inside and outside every being","Described only by paradox"],"L":["L3"],"say":"Lesson three. God is everywhere, yet beyond all description. He has no fixed form, yet perceives through every sense. He enjoys the modes of nature without being bound by them, and is at once inside and outside all beings. Words can only point.","start":220.08,"at":220.656,"end":238.104,"words":[[0.062,0.362,"Lesson"],[0.438,0.45,"three"],[1.275,0.225,"God"],[1.512,0.163,"is"],[1.688,0.65,"everywhere"],[2.362,0.312,"yet"],[2.688,0.425,"beyond"],[3.125,0.225,"all"],[3.362,0.7,"description"],[4.438,0.075,"He"],[4.525,0.175,"has"],[4.713,0.2,"no"],[4.925,0.338,"fixed"],[5.275,0.487,"form"],[6.013,0.3,"yet"],[6.325,0.562,"perceives"],[6.9,0.25,"through"],[7.162,0.275,"every"],[7.45,0.537,"sense"],[8.45,0.163,"He"],[8.625,0.487,"enjoys"],[9.125,0.087,"the"],[9.225,0.338,"modes"],[9.575,0.087,"of"],[9.675,0.45,"nature"],[10.137,0.35,"without"],[10.5,0.225,"being"],[10.738,0.312,"bound"],[11.062,0.175,"by"],[11.25,0.3,"them"],[11.863,0.2,"and"],[12.075,0.15,"is"],[12.238,0.125,"at"],[12.375,0.287,"once"],[12.675,0.537,"inside"],[13.225,0.113,"and"],[13.35,0.4,"outside"],[13.762,0.175,"all"],[13.95,0.463,"beings"],[14.8,0.362,"Words"],[15.175,0.188,"can"],[15.375,0.338,"only"],[15.725,0.487,"point"]]},{"layout":"lesson","headline":"Nature (Prakriti) and Spirit (Purusha) Are Both Beginningless","visual":["Matter and Spirit are both beginningless","Attachment to the gunas causes birth","Good and bad births follow from it"],"L":["L4"],"say":"Lesson four. Nature and Spirit are both beginningless. Matter and consciousness both have no beginning. The body comes from nature; the experience of pleasure and pain comes from the soul's association with it. And the soul's attachment to the modes of nature is what causes birth, in good wombs and bad.","start":238.104,"at":238.68,"end":259.224,"words":[[0.062,0.325,"Lesson"],[0.4,0.438,"four"],[1.2,0.487,"Nature"],[1.7,0.087,"and"],[1.8,0.525,"Spirit"],[2.35,0.188,"are"],[2.55,0.325,"both"],[2.888,0.787,"beginningless"],[4.075,0.45,"Matter"],[4.537,0.138,"and"],[4.688,0.738,"consciousness"],[5.438,0.312,"both"],[5.763,0.237,"have"],[6.013,0.212,"no"],[6.237,0.55,"beginning"],[7.175,0.087,"The"],[7.275,0.35,"body"],[7.638,0.3,"comes"],[7.95,0.175,"from"],[8.137,0.537,"nature"],[9.262,0.062,"the"],[9.338,0.588,"experience"],[9.938,0.125,"of"],[10.075,0.512,"pleasure"],[10.6,0.125,"and"],[10.738,0.45,"pain"],[11.2,0.338,"comes"],[11.55,0.175,"from"],[11.738,0.075,"the"],[11.825,0.425,"soul's"],[12.262,0.725,"association"],[13.0,0.163,"with"],[13.175,0.225,"it"],[13.812,0.138,"And"],[13.963,0.075,"the"],[14.05,0.4,"soul's"],[14.463,0.613,"attachment"],[15.088,0.113,"to"],[15.213,0.087,"the"],[15.312,0.35,"modes"],[15.675,0.1,"of"],[15.787,0.512,"nature"],[16.312,0.175,"is"],[16.5,0.175,"what"],[16.688,0.425,"causes"],[17.125,0.487,"birth"],[17.837,0.212,"in"],[18.062,0.212,"good"],[18.288,0.4,"wombs"],[18.7,0.15,"and"],[18.863,0.438,"bad"]]},{"layout":"lesson","headline":"Perceiving God Equally in All Beings Is the Highest Vision","visual":["The same Lord dwells equally in all","Whoever sees this harms no one","And reaches the supreme abode"],"L":["L5"],"say":"Lesson five. Perceiving God equally in all beings is the highest vision. Whoever sees the same eternal Lord in every mortal being truly sees. And because they see it, they injure no one, and they reach the highest.","start":259.224,"at":259.8,"end":274.488,"words":[[0.062,0.325,"Lesson"],[0.4,0.512,"five"],[1.312,0.5,"Perceiving"],[1.825,0.35,"God"],[2.2,0.55,"equally"],[2.763,0.15,"in"],[2.925,0.25,"all"],[3.188,0.412,"beings"],[3.612,0.188,"is"],[3.812,0.087,"the"],[3.913,0.45,"highest"],[4.375,0.463,"vision"],[5.237,0.388,"Whoever"],[5.638,0.425,"sees"],[6.075,0.087,"the"],[6.175,0.4,"same"],[6.588,0.475,"eternal"],[7.075,0.4,"Lord"],[7.5,0.175,"in"],[7.688,0.275,"every"],[7.975,0.362,"mortal"],[8.35,0.225,"being"],[8.588,0.362,"truly"],[8.963,0.5,"sees"],[9.863,0.113,"And"],[9.988,0.3,"because"],[10.3,0.125,"they"],[10.438,0.263,"see"],[10.713,0.237,"it"],[10.975,0.2,"they"],[11.188,0.338,"injure"],[11.537,0.212,"no"],[11.762,0.312,"one"],[12.1,0.163,"and"],[12.275,0.138,"they"],[12.425,0.287,"reach"],[12.725,0.087,"the"],[12.825,0.625,"highest"]]},{"layout":"steps","headline":"Five paths to freedom","visual":["Selfless service","Knowledge","Devotion","Meditation","Surrender"],"L":["L6"],"say":"Lesson six. Liberation is available through five paths. The soul can be freed through selfless service, through self-knowledge, through devotion, through meditation, or through surrender. All five lead to the same goal. Choose the one that fits your nature, and some, Krishna says, reach it simply by faith.","start":274.488,"at":275.064,"end":296.28,"words":[[0.075,0.312,"Lesson"],[0.4,0.512,"six"],[1.288,0.625,"Liberation"],[1.925,0.175,"is"],[2.112,0.575,"available"],[2.7,0.275,"through"],[2.987,0.338,"five"],[3.33